        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "The scripts are complete and verified. Here's a summary:\n\n**Created files in `/app/`:**\n1. **`compress.py`** - Reshards input directory into output directory with:\n   - Max 30 files per subdirectory (000/, 001/, etc.)\n   - Max 15MB per output file (part-XXXXX.jsonl)\n   - Creates a `manifest.json` mapping original files to their locations\n   - Usage: `python /app/compress.py <input_dir> <output_dir>`\n\n2. **`decompress.py`** - Reconstructs original files from resharded structure:\n   - Reads manifest.json to locate all file parts\n   - Extracts each original file at exact byte offsets\n   - Recreates original directory alongside resharded directory\n   - Usage: `python /app/decompress.py <resharded_dir>`\n\n3. **`pyproject.toml`** - uv-compatible package config with `uv sync` support\n\n**Verified with c4_sample/ (9,898 files, 800MB):**\n- ✅ Compress: Created 53 output files in 2 directories (30 + 23 files)\n- ✅ All output files ≤ 15MB\n- ✅ All directories ≤ 30 files\n- ✅ Decompress: Reconstructed all 9,898 files exactly\n- ✅ SHA256 checksums match perfectly\n- ✅ Works with `uv run python compress.py ...` and `uv run python decompress.py ...`",
